# What must NOT reach the build context.
#
# Docker matches these against the full path from the context root, so nested
# matches need `**/`. Everything a frozen install or a production build needs —
# `pnpm-lock.yaml`, every workspace `package.json`, `.npmrc`,
# `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, and all source — is deliberately absent from this file.

# --- Dependencies ---
# Installed inside the image from the committed lockfile. Copying the host's
# tree in would defeat that and can carry platform-specific native builds.
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# --- Build outputs ---
# Rebuilt inside the image; a stale host build must never be shipped.
**/dist
**/build
**/out
**/.next
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/next-env.d.ts

# --- Turborepo ---
**/.turbo

# --- Test and coverage artefacts ---
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/blob-report
**/.playwright

# --- Git metadata ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- Local environment files ---
# No image needs these, and none of them belongs in an image layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# --- Editor and OS metadata ---
.vscode
.idea
**/*.swp
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# --- Logs ---
**/*.log

# --- Docker's own files ---
# Read by the daemon directly, never needed inside an image.
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
compose.yaml
